    "space": {
      "$type": "dimension",
      "$description": "Four bands, ordered by how they answer density. `optical` is tied to stroke weight and cap height, not to layout — it holds constant at every density, because shrinking a 2px icon gap only makes the UI muddy. `inset` (control interiors) tightens gently, `stack` (grouping) more, `region`/`section`/`chapter` (page structure) hardest — that non-linearity is what separates a density mode from a zoom. Re-pointed wholesale by data-density. VALUES ARE ABSENT ON PURPOSE (decision D9): every step is DERIVED from the reading leading × density by `primitive.spaceScale` and injected at generate() time, the same way `text` fontSize is derived and injected. A step cannot be edited here without the scale that produced it — which is what stops spacing drifting back into a parallel authored table.",
      "hairline": {
        "$value": "2px"
      },
      "optical": {
        "$value": "4px"
      },
      "inset-2xs": {
        "$value": "6px"
