    "control": {
      "$type": "dimension",
      "$description": "Control box heights — buttons, inputs, avatars, icon buttons. A density mode that tightens padding but leaves control height alone is only half a mode, so these flip too. They compress more gently than page structure (~11%, against ~36%): a control's height is bounded below by its own line-height and by the pointer target, so it cannot follow the layout all the way down. Icon glyph sizes are NOT here — those hold, like the optical space band. `2xs` sits below the pointer-target floor on purpose: it is for read-only chips (badges, tags) that are never tapped, so the 24px minimum does not apply.",
