    "corner": {
      "$type": "cornerShape",
      "$description": "CORNER CURVATURE by role (FR-21), orthogonal to radius. Each family names a CSS `corner-shape` value the matching `rounded-{controls,containers,inline}` utility carries alongside its `border-radius`, so the corner can be a circular arc or a superellipse without any change to how big it is. `superellipse(1)` is a circular arc — the engine renders it identically to a bare `border-radius`, which is why these checked-in literals (the `arc` preset) reproduce today exactly and nothing curves until cornerSmoothing is rolled. `superellipse(2)` is the iOS squircle. Same three families as radius; circular is absent for the same reason AND because a superellipse on a rounded-full shape is a no-op. Web-render only: `corner-shape` is a paint-time property with no Figma-variable equivalent, so this group is excluded from figma-vars.json and token-map.json (see markdowns/FR-21-CORNER-SMOOTHING-SPIKE.md).",
